# Benefits

## Governance

Centralized metadata improves enterprise governance and consistency.

---

## Discoverability

Datasets become searchable and easier to understand.

---

## Reusability

Metadata is generated once and reused throughout the platform.

---

## Data Lineage

Provides the foundation for future lineage visualization and impact analysis.

---

## Platform Automation

Future platform capabilities can consume metadata directly instead of relying on manually maintained configuration.

---

## Scalability

Supports onboarding additional datasets without architectural redesign.

---

# Consequences

## Positive

- centralized metadata management
- improved governance
- reusable metadata services
- simplified dataset onboarding
- preparation for lineage
- improved maintainability

---

## Trade-offs

- additional storage
- metadata refresh operations
- catalog maintenance

These trade-offs are acceptable because metadata becomes a strategic enterprise asset.

---

# Alternatives Considered

## Notebook-Level Metadata

Rejected.

Reasons:

- duplicated logic
- inconsistent documentation
- difficult maintenance

---

## Manual Metadata Documentation

Rejected.

Reasons:

- quickly becomes outdated
- not machine-readable
- unsuitable for automation

---

## External Enterprise Catalog

Deferred.

Reasons:

Enterprise catalog products may be integrated in future production deployments.

The current framework establishes the architectural foundation while remaining lightweight and portable.

---

# Rationale

Metadata is one of the foundational capabilities of modern enterprise data platforms.

By elevating metadata to a managed platform service, the AI Workforce Capacity Planning Platform supports:

- Enterprise Data Governance
- Dataset Discovery
- Data Quality Certification
- Demand Intelligence
- Forecast Dataset Generation
- Future Feature Store integration
- Future Model Registry integration

The Metadata Framework also establishes a clear migration path toward enterprise governance solutions without changing downstream platform components.

---

# Decision Outcome

The AI Workforce Capacity Planning Platform formally adopts a centralized Enterprise Metadata Management Framework.

Metadata is treated as a governed platform asset rather than implementation-specific information.

Every dataset introduced into the platform must be profiled, cataloged, and registered before becoming available to downstream analytical or AI components.

